          "caption": "Part of plate 1, Baist's Real Estate Maps of Surveys of Seattle (1905). Shows building-by-building detail of the part of what is now the Pioneer Square neighborhood (then Seattle's commercial center), the adjacent railway tracks, and the Union Station development in the International District. The image covers between Occidental Way and Fifth Avenue South from just above King Street to Yesler Way. This shows the street layout before Second Avenue Extension was built south of Yesler Way.\n\nThis is a raw image of a plastic-covered document: some reflections and also some shadow.",
